      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Industry"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Industries process raw materials into higher-value secondary goods, forming the backbone of economic development.",
        "India's primary industrial zones include the Mumbai-Pune, Hugli, Bengaluru-Tamil Nadu, and Gujarat regions.",
        "Industrial location decisions depend on raw material availability, power supply, skilled labor, markets, and transport infrastructure.",
        "The 1991 Industrial Policy ushered in Liberalization, Privatization, and Globalization (LPG), fundamentally transforming Indian manufacturing."
      ],
      "id": "r777cvb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1chg8p8",
      "content": "• Industry refers to economic activities related to the production of goods."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "12zwog0",
      "content": "• It involves the conversion of raw materials into finished products."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nmfdtr4",
      "content": "• Industries help in increasing production and economic growth."
    },
